/Title (What is Morphological Parsing? Morphological Parsing is the process of analyzing a word to identify its smaller meaningful parts \(called morphemes\) and understand its grammatical properties. Example: Word: unhappiness un- = not happy = root word -ness = state or condition So, the word unhappiness means "the state of not being happy.")
